WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.900
RW Aurigae in two real SPHEREx images, a year apart. Is this change real?

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.900
A different wavelength can fake a change, so pairs too far apart are refused.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:14.800
HIPPARCHUS searches the archive, checks every exposure and compares like with like.

4
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.400
RW Aur got 2.56× brighter: 175σ formally, still 12.4σ with a 12.5% calibration floor.

5
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.200
The change holds in 24 of 24 analysis settings.

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.900
Barnard’s Star saturates SPHEREx: comparison refused.

7
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.900
Asteroid Kleopatra, tracked in real SPHEREx images, matches JPL Horizons. No Planet X.
